WEBVTT

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:07.480
Year 211 of the Third Galactic Empire

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:07.180
Is this your first time here, Prince?

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:09.610
Yeah, but I've heard about it a bunch of times.

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:11.560
It's even in our textbooks.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:19.290
That's the light of the runes!

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:29.340
Is this it?

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:31.850
Yes. This is Sakimori Academy.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:35.420
The cradle of our empire,

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:39.260
a land of curse and blessing.

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:26.390
Inuzuka...

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:30.250
What...

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:33.860
What am I supposed to do?

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:43.740
I'm not picking up any radio signal.

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:46.080
Is it because of the tetraquark radiation?

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:50.700
Judging from the position of the satellites,

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:53.000
this must be a fairly old crater that was formed by a graviton core.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:56.280
This means we're stuck in a 100km radius disc.

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.110
Communications are sealed off.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:02:59.280
There are no air supplies either.

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:02.250
The conclusion is—

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:06.860
Why am I even bothering?

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:11.170
I have no reason left to live.

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:26.140
I am Colonel Cain of the Dorssian Lunar Corps, in charge of the extermination of the type seven dangerous lifeforms.

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:31.890
We will proceed to guide Module 77 to the First Dorssian Sphere.

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:36.650
We finally got our hands on one, but we can't use it?

00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:40.460
Apparently, those students are the only ones able to pilot it.

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:42.170
And you're gonna believe that?

00:03:42.170 --> 00:03:42.910
Huh?

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:46.160
Colonel Cain piloted one, too, remember?

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:48.580
That's true...

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:55.180
So this is a Valvrave?

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:57.520
It's my first time seeing one close up.

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:00.260
Would you like to pilot it?

00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:05.230
Worry not.

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:11.850
As long as you follow the Council's directives and keep the Magius a secret, we can remain friends.

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:13.350
Friends?

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:16.870
That is right. Friends.

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:23.990
An enemy suit it may be, but beautiful it remains.

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:31.120
Cut that shit out, Sashinami!

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:35.370
We can't let you on board until we've confirmed that you're human!

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:37.600
Have you lost your goddamn mind?!

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:41.550
Is this how you repay Inuzuka's sacrifice?

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:43.320
I <i>am</i> grateful!

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:46.320
But letting anyone enter unchecked is out of the question.

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:48.010
You dumb bitch!

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:50.770
My duty is to protect the people.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:54.240
Is that how you repay trust?

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:56.090
Do you have any idea how much Haruto—

00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:57.020
That's enough.

00:04:57.020 --> 00:04:58.440
No, it's not!

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:02.190
Sashinami made the correct decision as a leader.

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:05.760
Do you think you could have done better, Yamada?

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:09.680
What choice did I have?

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:13.150
How could I trust someone who'd lied to me?

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:25.260
This isn't working, either.

00:05:26.390 --> 00:05:28.010
Maybe if I hooked up to another satellite...

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:30.660
It's pointless.

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:39.300
Thirty minutes of oxygen remaining.

00:05:44.630 --> 00:05:45.900
Rukino Saki.

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:49.780
You were there back then, too.

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:52.790
Who shot my eye?

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:01.060
It's just as you think.

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:05.210
L-Elf was possessed when he shot you.

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:07.240
I knew it.

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:11.080
L-Elf, you...

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:15.050
This country has changed.

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:18.650
In the beginning, the Dorssian military alliance

00:06:18.650 --> 00:06:24.330
was only a defense organization formed to counter the developed countries.

00:06:24.330 --> 00:06:26.730
Now, it's no different from the ARUS—

00:06:26.730 --> 00:06:30.620
No, it has already surpassed ARUS in greed and oppression.

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:34.250
Princes really do have a different way of viewing things.

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:37.260
My complaints do not stem from my royal blood,

00:06:37.260 --> 00:06:39.220
but rather from my identity as a Dorssian citizen.

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:42.330
That's why, L-Elf,

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:47.380
I intend to bring forth a revolution in Dorssia.

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:56.640
I know it's a dream too big for one man, but—

00:06:57.280 --> 00:06:59.290
That's not it, A-Drei.

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:04.090
I just happen to also be planning a revolution.

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:10.280
I couldn't believe in him to the end...

00:07:26.770 --> 00:07:27.890
L-Elf.

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:30.010
This is a signal flare!

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:34.520
Can you fix it? We could call for help—

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:37.030
Not a chance. Not without a power source for it.

00:07:40.630 --> 00:07:42.130
You want to be saved?

00:07:42.650 --> 00:07:45.180
Why are you trying to live?

00:07:45.180 --> 00:07:47.260
The other students are in danger!

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:48.610
I have to hurry back!

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:50.530
Are you still rambling on about that?

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:52.660
They abandoned you!

00:07:52.660 --> 00:07:54.760
Even Sashinami Shoko!

00:07:56.290 --> 00:07:59.410
<i>You're</i> the man-eating monsters!

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:02.000
Don't touch me, liar!

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:06.500
You've lied to me this entire time...

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:10.780
No! She...

00:08:10.780 --> 00:08:13.610
She only did it because she's the prime minister!

00:08:13.610 --> 00:08:15.550
Your behavior sickens me!

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:19.060
Tokishima Haruto, things will never go back to the way they used to be.

00:08:19.420 --> 00:08:21.640
You're a man-eater monster, now. An enemy of mankind!

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:22.100
No!

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:23.480
You're an enemy of Sashinami Shoko!

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:24.490
You're wrong!

00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:26.990
How am I wrong?!

00:08:26.990 --> 00:08:27.900
Face reality!

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:30.920
A reality <i>you</i> brought forth when you attacked us!

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:33.120
Don't place the blame on others.

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:37.020
It is your decisions alone that caused this.

00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:37.910
Damn it!

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:40.950
I keep on losing the people closest to me...

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:43.640
Inuzuka...

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:45.590
Marie and Aina...

00:08:45.590 --> 00:08:48.040
It's all... It's all your fault!

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:50.010
You're not the only one who's lost someone!

00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:51.880
Lieselotte is gone!

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:59.700
You're no exception! The world won't let you dream of a bright future!

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:02.860
There is no hope left!

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:05.690
You killed Sashinami Shoko's father!

00:09:07.340 --> 00:09:11.360
Remember when you destroyed the enemy fleet, before we arrived at the Moon?

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:15.360
Sashinami Shoko's father was on board.

00:09:19.570 --> 00:09:21.690
Why didn't you tell me?

00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:23.180
Why would I?

00:09:23.180 --> 00:09:24.620
It'd only make you suffer.

00:09:26.180 --> 00:09:28.520
I had no idea...

00:09:28.520 --> 00:09:30.360
Give up on her.

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:32.380
Your relationship can never be mended.

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:35.130
You're the monster that killed her father!

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:40.810
Let me make this clear.

00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:44.460
You stand no chance against me without the Valvrave.

00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:01.110
Yamada.

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:05.700
If the allied forces attack, protect Sashinami's ship.

00:10:06.180 --> 00:10:10.940
You think of me as so small a man that I'd discriminate those I save?

00:10:13.330 --> 00:10:16.740
<i>Ain't that true, Inuzuka?</i>

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:28.810
Is apple fine?

00:10:29.590 --> 00:10:31.240
Thanks...

00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:34.110
It's okay. Just tell me if you get hungry.

00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:36.090
Hey, Shoko...

00:10:37.110 --> 00:10:41.690
Did we do something wrong?

00:10:43.110 --> 00:10:45.880
Why is all of this happening to us?

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:50.790
We did nothing wrong. Nothing at all.

00:10:52.150 --> 00:10:54.070
Right...

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:16.650
We can't afford not to use the Valvraves.

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:19.130
Haruto won't return.

00:11:19.130 --> 00:11:20.820
It's my responsibility.

00:11:25.640 --> 00:11:27.100
"Resign as a human"?

00:11:27.890 --> 00:11:29.200
Press it already!

00:11:30.130 --> 00:11:32.610
I've been hungry since Haruto left!

00:11:32.610 --> 00:11:34.520
Do it! Do it!

00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:38.340
Haruto? Haruto pressed this button?

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:41.230
Yeah. For revenge.

00:11:41.230 --> 00:11:43.130
He said it was to avenge someone.

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:46.600
What was her name? Sh... Shoko?

00:11:48.550 --> 00:11:51.100
Resign as a human?

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:52.520
That's right.

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:55.110
It won't move if you're human.

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:58.360
It won't move? The Valvrave?

00:11:58.360 --> 00:11:59.590
That's right.

00:11:59.590 --> 00:12:03.610
Let's see... It was on the first day...

00:12:06.690 --> 00:12:07.870
There it is!

00:12:08.440 --> 00:12:10.660
Move!

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:12.160
You're a robot! Move, dammit!

00:12:12.670 --> 00:12:16.090
I owe this to Shoko! Please!

00:12:17.190 --> 00:12:19.590
Haruto, don't tell me...

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:30.030
You did it for me?

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:35.310
Stop it! I won't let anyone touch the Valvrave!

00:12:37.250 --> 00:12:38.440
Haruto...

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:55.040
I've hated you from the beginning.

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:58.190
You've always looked down on me!

00:12:58.190 --> 00:13:01.420
Half, my ass! You say the same thing as Lieselotte!

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:07.430
If you're so damn smart, why did we end up like this?

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:12.020
If I had a Valvrave, I could've saved Lieselotte!

00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:13.400
You damn monster!

00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:16.520
Why are you so dead set on surviving?!

00:13:16.840 --> 00:13:20.440
You living means other people have to die!

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:25.650
Why don't you follow through with your idiotic ideal about saving people and die here?!

00:13:28.760 --> 00:13:33.120
Your dear princess was also one of those monsters!

00:13:33.120 --> 00:13:33.980
What?!

00:13:33.980 --> 00:13:36.400
Lieselotte was a Magius!

00:13:36.400 --> 00:13:37.860
What a poor lie!

00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:40.270
If she was a Magius, why would she be imprisoned?

00:13:40.270 --> 00:13:41.920
Because she sided with humans!

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:43.920
That's what brought the wrath of the Council upon her.

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:45.160
What Council?

00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:48.050
An organization to keep the Magius a secret from the world!

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:49.920
Am I supposed to believe this?

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:55.230
Do you really think just anybody could have built the Phantom and manipulated the UN?

00:13:55.980 --> 00:13:58.380
The girl you loved was a Magius!

00:13:58.380 --> 00:13:59.360
Silence!

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:03.480
She lived much longer than you. She was immortal.

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:06.490
She was a monster who devoured humans!

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:10.240
Shut up! Shut up!

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:11.620
Shut up!

00:14:27.930 --> 00:14:31.470
<i>Lieselotte! Could you really have been a Magius?</i>

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:38.430
<i>An immortal creature that lives on for centuries! The top of the food chain!</i>

00:14:38.430 --> 00:14:41.360
<i>And I would try to save you?</i>

00:14:45.560 --> 00:14:47.630
<i>It's not even funny!</i>

00:14:51.720 --> 00:14:52.840
<i>Tears?</i>

00:14:53.440 --> 00:14:54.660
<i>I see.</i>

00:14:55.090 --> 00:14:57.000
<i>I bring grief everywhere I go.</i>

00:14:58.070 --> 00:14:59.330
<i>And not just to L-Elf...</i>

00:15:00.480 --> 00:15:04.250
<i>Is that why I'm being punished?</i>

00:15:08.610 --> 00:15:10.930
Good enough, Haruto.

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:13.990
Inuzuka?

00:15:14.960 --> 00:15:17.750
You did what you could.

00:15:18.760 --> 00:15:21.080
You're allowed a break.

00:15:21.080 --> 00:15:24.860
That world is all sadness and pain.

00:15:26.420 --> 00:15:29.360
Did I do well?

00:15:30.020 --> 00:15:33.120
Yeah. Pretty well.

00:15:34.020 --> 00:15:35.100
Thanks.

00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:40.040
I guess I wanted to hear someone tell me that.

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:56.990
Me?

00:16:03.260 --> 00:16:06.400
<i>A prisoner? I couldn't have been more mistaken.</i>

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:09.570
<i>You were one of them all along!</i>

00:16:09.980 --> 00:16:11.930
Because she sided with humans!

00:16:11.930 --> 00:16:14.120
That's what brought the wrath of the Council upon her.

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:15.990
<i>No...</i>

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:19.750
<i>Lieselotte really was a prisoner.</i>

00:16:23.420 --> 00:16:28.990
<i>Why would she side with humans? My only clues are her words.</i>

00:16:29.450 --> 00:16:30.400
<i>And her actions.</i>

00:16:30.990 --> 00:16:34.180
<i>She helped us and the royalists.</i>

00:16:34.930 --> 00:16:38.320
This is it. This is the end of my story.

00:16:38.320 --> 00:16:39.830
Then you'll die in vain.

00:16:40.610 --> 00:16:45.280
You were so desperate you even became a holy spirit. What a waste.

00:16:45.280 --> 00:16:46.600
That's not it!

00:16:46.600 --> 00:16:49.770
Why do you think I was born?

00:16:50.770 --> 00:16:54.210
To have my body tweaked and toyed with like a guinea pig?

00:16:54.210 --> 00:16:55.420
No!

00:16:55.420 --> 00:16:57.130
To pilot the Valvrave, then?

00:16:57.130 --> 00:16:58.080
To kill people?

00:16:58.080 --> 00:16:59.410
Of course not!

00:16:59.810 --> 00:17:02.160
Then why?

00:17:04.280 --> 00:17:07.960
<i>Lieselotte probably lived for centuries as a Magius.</i>

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:10.060
<i>Why would she side with humans?</i>

00:17:10.060 --> 00:17:12.050
<i>What happened to you?</i>

00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:14.890
Mikhail...

00:17:16.710 --> 00:17:20.710
You're so... young.

00:17:23.080 --> 00:17:26.980
There is no safe haven for us.

00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:35.140
Were you trying to make a haven?

00:17:35.780 --> 00:17:38.740
For mankind and the Magius?

00:17:39.420 --> 00:17:41.940
My runes are already disappearing.

00:17:41.940 --> 00:17:43.120
Time is running out.

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:44.570
Exactly.

00:17:45.110 --> 00:17:48.130
That's why you need to leave a mark in the world.

00:17:48.660 --> 00:17:52.800
There are still things that you can do.

00:17:53.270 --> 00:17:56.060
I cannot live my life with you,

00:17:56.060 --> 00:17:59.800
but I can inherit your dream.

00:18:00.370 --> 00:18:03.160
Giving up on life takes a huge weight off my shoulders.

00:18:04.200 --> 00:18:06.810
It doesn't matter what others think of me.

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:09.810
The only thing that does is what <i>I</i> want to do.

00:18:09.810 --> 00:18:11.320
So that's why...

00:18:11.810 --> 00:18:13.160
...I can't die just yet!

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:19.450
L-Elf!

00:18:22.550 --> 00:18:24.040
What?

00:18:24.460 --> 00:18:26.490
What was that?

00:18:30.180 --> 00:18:32.540
Tokishima Haruto, what was that?

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:35.310
I don't know, but that light...

00:18:35.310 --> 00:18:38.730
Cain did the same thing.

00:18:38.730 --> 00:18:43.450
We shouldn't be surprised that you are able to do the same as a Magius...

00:18:44.180 --> 00:18:47.930
L-Elf, could this power somehow save us?

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:51.940
You might be able to ignite that flare you had earlier.

00:18:52.840 --> 00:18:53.900
L-Elf.

00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:56.350
I realized that I still love everyone.

00:18:57.140 --> 00:18:58.450
I want to laugh together with them again.

00:18:58.800 --> 00:19:02.420
Let's make a world where man and your kind can live together.

00:19:03.990 --> 00:19:06.520
This time it won't be just a replacement for JIOR.

00:19:06.520 --> 00:19:09.580
It will be ours. A country just for us!

00:19:11.200 --> 00:19:14.330
The light that Cain used was probably runes.

00:19:14.330 --> 00:19:17.630
It can be activated by information in the form of words.

00:19:17.630 --> 00:19:19.260
A spell of some sort?

00:19:19.260 --> 00:19:19.980
But...

00:19:19.980 --> 00:19:22.760
You just did something similar to that.

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:26.140
It might not be perfect, but it was enough to make it work.

00:19:30.140 --> 00:19:32.080
Even if someone does see this flare,

00:19:32.090 --> 00:19:34.000
we can't know if it'll be friend or foe.

00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:37.520
It's a gamble, and the odds aren't in our favor.

00:19:37.520 --> 00:19:39.930
But they aren't zero.

00:19:41.380 --> 00:19:43.340
L-Elf, let's do it.

00:19:43.340 --> 00:19:44.160
Yeah.

00:19:45.090 --> 00:19:46.200
I...

00:19:46.610 --> 00:19:47.660
...can't die just yet!

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:10.000
A world where humans and those with the holy spirit can live together, huh?

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:12.000
It'll be a long struggle.

00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:13.450
It's gonna be fine.

00:20:13.450 --> 00:20:15.020
You have a plan.

00:20:15.020 --> 00:20:15.650
Nope.

00:20:15.650 --> 00:20:16.790
Hey, now...

00:20:16.790 --> 00:20:19.680
We'll figure something out together.

00:20:19.680 --> 00:20:21.490
You mean the students?

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:23.360
The whole world.

00:20:23.360 --> 00:20:28.160
But for that to happen, they have to learn about the Magius and the Council of One Hundred and One.

00:20:28.520 --> 00:20:32.330
I see. So you want to unveil the world?

00:20:32.690 --> 00:20:35.330
I burned my hands trying to keep secrets.

00:20:36.450 --> 00:20:37.550
L-Elf.

00:20:37.550 --> 00:20:38.560
What?

00:20:38.560 --> 00:20:41.640
You don't have any more secrets to keep from me.

00:20:43.350 --> 00:20:44.120
Nope.

00:20:46.100 --> 00:20:47.300
Neither do I.

00:20:51.680 --> 00:20:53.030
There!

00:20:53.030 --> 00:20:54.190
Yeah.

00:21:01.210 --> 00:21:04.220
Located a type seven dangerous lifeform and a deserter!

00:21:04.220 --> 00:21:08.330
As per the UN's regulations regarding dangerous lifeforms, we will proceed with their extermination!

00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:13.840
Things have always been complicated between the two of us.

00:21:13.840 --> 00:21:16.960
We're total opposites.

00:21:29.230 --> 00:21:30.460
Unit 4?!

00:21:30.460 --> 00:21:31.600
Rukino!

00:21:33.610 --> 00:21:35.670
Haruto! And L-Elf!

00:21:36.530 --> 00:21:39.060
There! I found them!

00:21:43.070 --> 00:21:45.570
It's a type seven dangerous lifeform! Take it out!

00:21:52.200 --> 00:21:53.610
Tokishima Haruto.

00:21:53.610 --> 00:21:57.120
Let's make a pact to unveil the world.

00:21:57.750 --> 00:21:59.780
No, L-Elf.

00:22:00.400 --> 00:22:01.750
This isn't a pact.

00:22:04.480 --> 00:22:05.980
It's called a promise.

00:22:23.090 --> 00:22:24.310
L-Elf...

00:22:24.900 --> 00:22:28.420
H-Neun, now you.

00:22:29.120 --> 00:22:31.340
What on Earth is going on here?

00:22:32.400 --> 00:22:34.260
This isn't betrayal.

00:22:35.610 --> 00:22:39.420
This is my punishment.

00:24:11.930 --> 00:24:17.100
PREVIEW

00:24:13.260 --> 00:24:19.260
